\f0\fs32\b Screen Layout\b0\fs24\par
\par
The game window is divided into a map area and a bottom message area. The map uses one character-sized cell per terrain square; the message area is a three-row HUD split into left and right columns.\par
\par
\f1
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par
| Map Area                                                               |\par
|                                                                        |\par
|  terrain, cities, units, waypoints, fog of war                         |\par
|  units/cities needing attention flash in place                         |\par
|                                                                        |\par
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par
| Attention                         | Status: pause/round/orders/counts   |\par
| Warning                           | Inspector summary                   |\par
| Command response                  | Inspector detail                    |\par
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+\par
\f0\par
\fs28\b Map Area\b0\fs24\par
\par
\b Terrain\b0 - sea is blue, land is brown, free cities are white, player cities are green, computer cities are red, and unexplored cells are black.\par
\par
\b Units\b0 - player units use uppercase letters, computer units use lowercase letters. Unit colors show mode: awake units are white, sentries are pink, exploring units are light green, coastline-follow ships are dark green, and moving or sleeping units are black.\par
\par
\b Attention flash\b0 - the current unit or city waiting for input flashes on the map. Cities needing production show ?.\par
\par
\b Waypoints\b0 - waypoint markers are shown on land cells and can carry marching orders.\par
\par
\fs28\b Message Area\b0\fs24\par
\par
The bottom HUD is five text rows tall, with three active rows. The left column uses about 55% of the width for player-facing messages. The right column uses the remaining width for stable game status and mouse inspection.\par
\par
\f1
+-----------------------------------+------------------------------------+\par
| Attention                         | Status                             |\par
| Warning                           | Inspector Summary                  |\par
| Command Response                  | Inspector Detail                   |\par
+-----------------------------------+------------------------------------+\par
\f0\par
\b Attention\b0 - gold text. Shows the unit or city currently asking for orders, such as a fighter needing fuel, a city needing production, or an army ready to move.\par
\par
\b Warning\b0 - red text. Shows blocked moves, failed actions, combat outcomes, crashes, illegal production choices, and other urgent feedback.\par
\par
\b Command Response\b0 - light blue text. Shows successful commands and confirmations, such as marching orders, flight paths, save/load messages, docking, landing, and waypoint changes.\par
\par
\b Status\b0 - gray text. Shows pause state, round number, handicap countdown when active, debug map mode, destination or current order context, and a compact production/exploration summary.\par
\par
\b Inspector Summary\b0 - gray text. Shows the primary mouse-over summary for the cell under the cursor, usually coordinates plus terrain, city, or unit.\par
\par
\b Inspector Detail\b0 - gray text. Shows secondary mouse-over detail such as fuel, cargo, production, docked ships, missions, orders, or target coordinates.\par
}
